  "outlookText": "000\nACPN50 PHFO 051146\nTWOCP \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS Central Pacific Hurricane Center Honolulu HI\nIssued by NWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM HST Thu Nov 05 2026\n\nFor the central North Pacific...between 140W and 180W:\n\nWell Southeast of the Hawaiian Islands (CP95):\nShowers and thunderstorms continue to show signs of organization in\nassociation with an area of low pressure located over the eastern\nportion of the Central Pacific basin. While earlier satellite wind\ndata suggested the system does not yet have a well-defined\ncirculation, environmental conditions appear conducive for\nadditional development. A tropical depression is now likely to form\nover the next day or so while the system moves westward to\nwest-northwestward at 10 to 15 mph, passing well south of the\nHawaiian Islands.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...high...80 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...high...80 percent.\n\n$$\nForecaster Papin\nNNNN",
